1
00:00:00,208 --> 00:00:01,209
[Previously]

2
00:00:01,338 --> 00:00:02,920
We usually leave girls alone.

3
00:00:03,056 --> 00:00:04,656
But when it comes to the Monchaitrakuls,

4
00:00:04,773 --> 00:00:07,060
no one's getting spared.
Not even women or children.

5
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:08,960
Someone actually died

6
00:00:08,997 --> 00:00:11,160
because of the feud
between our two families,

7
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,800
Uncle Wirat, Pakkard's father.

8
00:00:14,147 --> 00:00:16,360
You have to cut ties with that family.

9
00:00:16,899 --> 00:00:20,000
I understand if you
don't want to be with me.

10
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:23,440
They made this mess. Let them deal with it.

11
00:00:35,731 --> 00:00:37,211
If I'd gotten there in time that day,

12
00:00:37,779 --> 00:00:39,099
your father might still be alive.

13
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:41,160
Did you know beforehand

14
00:00:42,134 --> 00:00:43,534
that something was going to happen?

15
00:00:44,854 --> 00:00:45,920
I know those people well.

16
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:49,600
They may act generous toward the villagers,

17
00:00:50,278 --> 00:00:53,440
but they've always played dirty.

18
00:00:58,302 --> 00:01:00,120
But we don't have any proof.

19
00:01:01,099 --> 00:01:04,480
I think some things
should be left in the past.

20
00:01:06,704 --> 00:01:10,205
Then leave this matter to the adults.

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,500
"Juliet and Juliet"
(Episode 4)

22
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:25,601
ANNA SIRIN KONGPURIM

23
00:02:25,624 --> 00:02:27,384
Mom would be so
happy if she could see this.

24
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:29,521
You know

25
00:02:30,851 --> 00:02:33,000
how much she loved white roses, don't you?

26
00:02:36,835 --> 00:02:38,360
How would she know, Dad?

27
00:02:39,816 --> 00:02:41,600
She's never even seen Mom's face in person.

28
00:02:42,931 --> 00:02:44,700
But she looks exactly like Mom.

29
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,280
All she has to do is look in the mirror.

30
00:02:49,081 --> 00:02:50,241
Isn't that right, sweetheart?

31
00:02:54,104 --> 00:02:55,560
The saddest day of my life

32
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,680
was the day I couldn't protect your mother

33
00:02:59,534 --> 00:03:00,900
when the accident happened.

34
00:03:03,502 --> 00:03:05,560
I won't let anything
like that happen again.

35
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,541
As long as I can keep an eye on you,

36
00:03:13,275 --> 00:03:14,755
I won't have anything to worry about.

37
00:03:22,643 --> 00:03:23,644
Tokyo.

38
00:03:26,152 --> 00:03:28,520
You're not involved
with that family's daughter, are you?

39
00:03:34,971 --> 00:03:36,400
What do you mean, Dad?

40
00:03:37,468 --> 00:03:38,520
Exactly what I said.

41
00:03:40,337 --> 00:03:43,080
Seeing her, talking to her,

42
00:03:43,580 --> 00:03:44,620
or being friends with her.

43
00:03:45,886 --> 00:03:47,650
You're not doing any of that, are you?

44
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,700
We're just in the same class. That's all.

45
00:04:07,010 --> 00:04:09,170
I don't want to have to
watch my back around outsiders

46
00:04:10,350 --> 00:04:12,520
and then be suspicious
of my own family too.

47
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:16,960
If you promise me,

48
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,321
I'll trust you.

49
00:04:24,990 --> 00:04:25,991
I promise.

50
00:04:28,718 --> 00:04:30,200
I won't let you down, Dad.

51
00:05:15,174 --> 00:05:16,175
Boss.

52
00:05:16,939 --> 00:05:19,019
The situation at our port
still hasn't settled down.

53
00:05:19,755 --> 00:05:20,756
The other night,

54
00:05:21,195 --> 00:05:24,160
people were still sneaking
in and causing trouble.

55
00:05:25,051 --> 00:05:28,052
And that's not even counting
those spreading rumors

56
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:30,400
to frighten the villagers.

57
00:05:30,453 --> 00:05:32,853
The community leaders
have been resigning one after another.

58
00:05:33,816 --> 00:05:34,817
What should we do, Boss?

59
00:05:37,198 --> 00:05:38,760
Throw money at the problem for now.

60
00:05:39,827 --> 00:05:41,400
Whatever they want, pay them.

61
00:05:42,334 --> 00:05:45,640
Right now, we need as many villagers
on our side as possible.

62
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:47,361
Yes, Boss.

63
00:05:51,246 --> 00:05:52,280
And what about Blue?

64
00:05:54,984 --> 00:05:57,520
I'm not letting that matter go.

65
00:06:41,184 --> 00:06:43,960
Dude, is that a real kiss
or just the camera angle?

66
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:51,000
Why are you zooming in so much?

67
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:52,601
Zooming in won't change anything.

68
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:54,130
I told you, I saw it with my own eyes.

69
00:06:54,910 --> 00:06:57,400
What do we do? Should we tell Yi?

70
00:06:57,715 --> 00:06:58,716
Damn it.

71
00:06:59,534 --> 00:07:01,360
Why the hell did they have to get together?

72
00:07:01,710 --> 00:07:03,211
Don't their families hate each other?

73
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:06,100
What, are they trying
to be Romeo and Juliet?

74
00:07:07,134 --> 00:07:09,100
So what are we doing?
Are we telling Yi or not?

75
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:11,200
How the hell should I know?

76
00:07:13,486 --> 00:07:14,487
Here.

77
00:07:15,758 --> 00:07:16,859
And this pile too.

78
00:07:17,475 --> 00:07:19,380
Put them in the right shelves, okay?

79
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:44,240
My dad's getting suspicious.

80
00:07:44,770 --> 00:07:46,680
We'll have to be more careful for a while.

81
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,001
Okay.

82
00:08:07,131 --> 00:08:08,480
- I should go.
- Okay.

83
00:08:15,243 --> 00:08:16,244
Come on. Let's go.

84
00:08:28,411 --> 00:08:30,171
Chanthara Suksa has sent us

85
00:08:30,230 --> 00:08:33,800
its list of representatives for
this year's friendship event.

86
00:08:33,867 --> 00:08:36,088
As for Chantrarawatthana,

87
00:08:36,102 --> 00:08:39,200
I've put Tokyo's name down, Principal.

88
00:08:39,456 --> 00:08:41,600
How much did he contribute last year?

89
00:08:42,278 --> 00:08:44,800
They provided a budget of two million baht.

90
00:08:46,064 --> 00:08:47,920
Then let's ask for a little more this year.

91
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:50,800
Tokyo is already in Grade 12.

92
00:08:51,987 --> 00:08:54,587
If the event isn't grand enough to
live up to the Kongpurim name,

93
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:56,600
I don't think that would look good.

94
00:08:57,638 --> 00:08:59,880
Can Mr. Po still afford it, Principal?

95
00:09:00,096 --> 00:09:02,840
He's been strapped for cash
since he lost the port concession.

96
00:09:02,997 --> 00:09:06,557
His men have been collecting interest from
the local vendors more aggressively than ever.

97
00:09:07,155 --> 00:09:08,440
Does that include you?

98
00:09:09,294 --> 00:09:11,400
Yes, but I'm not the only one.

99
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:14,476
Some teachers can't keep up with their
teachers' cooperative loan payments either.

100
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:17,900
Mr. Po has tightened his purse strings and
stopped lending them money to stay afloat.

101
00:09:18,501 --> 00:09:21,619
Then why don't we put
Phakjira in charge of the students

102
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:23,619
for this event instead?

103
00:09:23,976 --> 00:09:28,277
After all, her father is
about to replace Mr. Po.

104
00:09:28,512 --> 00:09:30,708
He should be able to support our budget.

105
00:09:31,051 --> 00:09:34,000
But will Mr. Wiboon be
as generous as Mr. Po?

106
00:09:34,742 --> 00:09:37,000
There's no harm in trying.

107
00:09:37,073 --> 00:09:40,920
After all, the one person we know
is short on cash is Mr. Po.

108
00:09:42,074 --> 00:09:43,475
[ School Principal ]

109
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:45,800
All right. Here's what we'll do.

110
00:09:49,011 --> 00:09:50,012
What?

111
00:09:50,366 --> 00:09:51,880
Why does it have to be me again?

112
00:09:52,915 --> 00:09:55,240
You already made me do
the bulletin board last time.

113
00:09:56,700 --> 00:09:59,500
It's not just you. I've assigned Tokyo too.

114
00:10:00,470 --> 00:10:02,120
You'll be working as a pair.

115
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:04,381
I'm not asking you to do it alone.

116
00:10:14,502 --> 00:10:15,742
What do you think we should do?

117
00:10:17,115 --> 00:10:18,160
Hmm.

118
00:10:19,163 --> 00:10:20,600
There are so many details.

119
00:10:22,446 --> 00:10:24,920
Can we finish it in time
with so few people?

120
00:10:29,544 --> 00:10:32,240
And this is the friendship event.

121
00:10:32,424 --> 00:10:34,384
Are these really all the
people who came to help?

122
00:10:37,832 --> 00:10:39,760
Who wants to work for free?

123
00:10:41,416 --> 00:10:43,776
They're probably off flirting with boys
from other schools.

124
00:10:48,014 --> 00:10:51,160
Then let's hurry up and get this done.

125
00:10:53,507 --> 00:10:55,800
Blue, I'm sorry, but...

126
00:10:56,104 --> 00:10:58,250
if we finish helping today,

127
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,401
could you ask your father

128
00:11:00,411 --> 00:11:02,200
to let my dad work at the port again?

129
00:11:03,278 --> 00:11:04,299
And for me,

130
00:11:04,478 --> 00:11:06,720
could you talk to the teacher
who gave me an Incomplete?

131
00:11:09,560 --> 00:11:11,675
Wait. What exactly does everyone think

132
00:11:11,835 --> 00:11:13,160
I can help you with?

133
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:16,520
Doesn't your father run the port?

134
00:11:16,811 --> 00:11:19,360
If we can't ask you for
help, who else can we ask?

135
00:11:20,170 --> 00:11:22,400
Can't you even do this
much for your friends?

136
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,920
I can't help any of you.

137
00:11:28,587 --> 00:11:30,920
I came here today to
design the Moon Night stage.

138
00:11:32,640 --> 00:11:34,560
If you came expecting
anything else, just leave.

139
00:11:39,896 --> 00:11:40,897
Huh?

140
00:11:50,283 --> 00:11:51,284
It's okay.

141
00:11:52,084 --> 00:11:53,360
I'll lend a hand too.

142
00:11:55,866 --> 00:11:59,240
With so few people, we'll only have
a wooden frame by the day of the event.

143
00:12:10,451 --> 00:12:12,280
What are we going to do?

144
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,520
Why don't you let us help?

145
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:17,760
What? Why are you scooting away?

146
00:12:18,307 --> 00:12:21,160
Why are you squeezing in with us?
Just stay where you were.

147
00:12:26,942 --> 00:12:29,120
Come on. Everyone knows
about you two already.

148
00:12:29,214 --> 00:12:32,040
Yeah. You're the only one
who never thought to tell your friends.

149
00:12:32,243 --> 00:12:33,244
Yeah.

150
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:35,440
You two already knew?

151
00:12:40,819 --> 00:12:41,820
Go on.

152
00:12:43,203 --> 00:12:44,204
I'm sorry.

153
00:12:45,859 --> 00:12:48,040
I just didn't know how to bring it up.

154
00:12:48,486 --> 00:12:50,230
You could've just told us.

155
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:51,721
Exactly.

156
00:12:59,283 --> 00:13:02,563
But you know what my family is like.

157
00:13:02,595 --> 00:13:05,320
Yeah, I know. I know everything.

158
00:13:05,507 --> 00:13:07,680
Yi told the two of us

159
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,440
to keep an eye on you and Blue.

160
00:13:09,843 --> 00:13:12,798
Yi even used our parents to threaten us.

161
00:13:13,187 --> 00:13:14,188
That's right.

162
00:13:15,624 --> 00:13:17,200
Don't look at me like that.

163
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:19,980
I've applied for a part-time job
in case I need to help my parents.

164
00:13:20,104 --> 00:13:22,300
And in case Yi ever
comes to collect the debt,

165
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:24,280
we'd be screwed. What
else was I supposed to do?

166
00:13:24,587 --> 00:13:26,144
Exactly. And one more thing.

167
00:13:26,166 --> 00:13:28,280
We're not friends with
you because of your money,

168
00:13:28,300 --> 00:13:29,712
no matter what everyone else says.

169
00:13:35,448 --> 00:13:36,640
Oh my goodness.

170
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:44,720
Thank you.

171
00:13:47,085 --> 00:13:48,086
Not so fast.

172
00:13:48,230 --> 00:13:51,720
Don't tell Yi
that we already know.

173
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:53,401
Keep it quiet.

174
00:13:55,472 --> 00:13:56,473
Okay, okay.

175
00:14:13,110 --> 00:14:14,280
Give them a hug too.

176
00:14:30,056 --> 00:14:31,438
Oh, perfect timing.

177
00:14:32,350 --> 00:14:34,160
Come here, sweetheart. Come on.

178
00:14:43,224 --> 00:14:44,225
Here she is.

179
00:14:47,918 --> 00:14:50,120
You said you wanted
to study in London, right?

180
00:14:50,563 --> 00:14:52,560
So I hired a tutor to
give you a trial lesson.

181
00:14:58,280 --> 00:14:59,281
Yes,

182
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:02,150
but what I meant was that I
wanted to study in London.

183
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,181
Just try it and see if you like it.

184
00:15:05,606 --> 00:15:07,000
If you really do,

185
00:15:07,163 --> 00:15:10,043
I'll hire someone to design a whole
curriculum and teach you right here.

186
00:15:10,430 --> 00:15:12,160
That way, you won't have to go so far away.

187
00:15:16,958 --> 00:15:18,680
Come, have a seat.

188
00:15:19,480 --> 00:15:20,481
You should talk to her.

189
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,920
Please take good care of my daughter.

190
00:15:27,296 --> 00:15:28,297
Of course.

191
00:15:32,686 --> 00:15:35,806
Should we start by getting
to know each other better?

192
00:15:37,566 --> 00:15:38,567
Okay.

193
00:15:39,144 --> 00:15:41,100
Which literary works do you like most?

194
00:15:45,115 --> 00:15:46,280
Romeo &amp; Juliet.

195
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,086
Great choice.

196
00:15:50,360 --> 00:15:52,120
What about Hamlet?

197
00:15:55,102 --> 00:15:56,400
I've read all of this.

198
00:16:03,616 --> 00:16:05,720
Is that enough to step outside

199
00:16:06,491 --> 00:16:08,100
and learn from the real world?

200
00:16:10,094 --> 00:16:11,640
With a strong purpose in your heart,

201
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:13,880
you can find out who you want to be

202
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,361
wherever you are.

203
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:27,040
What's wrong?

204
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:47,880
Whoa, you're a pretty good shot.

205
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,226
That's because I had a good teacher.

206
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:52,990
True. A good teacher—and handsome too.

207
00:16:54,872 --> 00:16:57,320
You just got a new gun.
Why don't you try your old one?

208
00:16:58,371 --> 00:16:59,619
- You think?
- Yeah.

209
00:17:09,064 --> 00:17:10,065
You're right.

210
00:17:11,080 --> 00:17:13,240
Then you can have my new one.
I don't want it anymore.

211
00:17:14,707 --> 00:17:16,400
What would I even use it for?

212
00:17:17,347 --> 00:17:19,120
I don't want to grow up to be like you.

213
00:17:19,148 --> 00:17:21,600
Wow. Listen to you.

214
00:17:26,107 --> 00:17:27,340
- Yi.
- Yeah?

215
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:28,800
I'm seriously asking.

216
00:17:30,464 --> 00:17:32,424
Have you ever wanted to
try doing something else?

217
00:17:33,456 --> 00:17:35,336
Something that doesn't
involve working for Dad?

218
00:17:37,432 --> 00:17:38,433
No, never.

219
00:17:40,862 --> 00:17:41,880
But I do.

220
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,520
Then do whatever you want.

221
00:17:47,616 --> 00:17:48,617
Dad won't stop you.

222
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,960
But do you really have to leave home?

223
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:54,101
If I never leave,

224
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:55,984
how will I find out what I truly enjoy?

225
00:17:56,050 --> 00:17:58,050
How will I discover my dream
or what I want to do?

226
00:17:58,251 --> 00:17:59,252
I have to leave.

227
00:18:00,122 --> 00:18:01,400
I've never had to leave home,

228
00:18:01,423 --> 00:18:03,263
but I still know what I
want and what I enjoy.

229
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:06,780
But you didn't choose any of it yourself.

230
00:18:06,904 --> 00:18:07,960
Dad chose it for you.

231
00:18:11,624 --> 00:18:13,625
Shooting. Boxing.

232
00:18:13,955 --> 00:18:16,000
Running gambling dens. Collecting debts.

233
00:18:17,624 --> 00:18:19,625
Did Dad ever ask if you
wanted to do any of that?

234
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:22,241
No.

235
00:18:23,251 --> 00:18:25,091
Maybe Dad made you
do those things for so long

236
00:18:25,144 --> 00:18:26,864
that you convinced yourself you liked them.

237
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:31,101
But I think I really do like them.

238
00:18:31,601 --> 00:18:32,640
I honestly feel

239
00:18:33,134 --> 00:18:34,880
like I was born for this.

240
00:18:38,392 --> 00:18:39,720
Then you're lucky.

241
00:18:41,389 --> 00:18:44,200
You didn't choose it, but
you still ended up liking it.

242
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:46,001
Okay.

243
00:18:46,414 --> 00:18:47,500
But for me,

244
00:18:48,526 --> 00:18:49,886
I don't think this life is for me.

245
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:53,240
I think I need to choose for myself.

246
00:18:53,886 --> 00:18:54,887
I don't want this.

247
00:18:57,192 --> 00:18:58,912
Do you really want to go abroad that badly?

248
00:19:09,766 --> 00:19:10,767
Fine.

249
00:19:11,232 --> 00:19:12,320
I'll talk to Dad for you.

250
00:19:13,675 --> 00:19:14,925
- You will?
- Yeah.

251
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,840
Make sure you find out what your dream is.

252
00:19:18,518 --> 00:19:20,160
- Really?
- Sure.

253
00:19:37,099 --> 00:19:38,240
You're healed now.

254
00:19:43,848 --> 00:19:46,158
Hey, tell me something.

255
00:19:46,840 --> 00:19:48,560
How did you figure out what your dream was?

256
00:19:49,960 --> 00:19:51,800
What made you ask me that?

257
00:19:54,630 --> 00:19:56,480
I want to have a dream like you do.

258
00:19:58,371 --> 00:20:00,680
Have you loved drawing
since you were little?

259
00:20:06,998 --> 00:20:09,158
It was a long time ago.
You're better off not knowing.

260
00:20:10,075 --> 00:20:12,760
Why? Can't you tell me?

261
00:20:13,371 --> 00:20:14,720
Please tell me.

262
00:20:15,248 --> 00:20:16,249
Please?

263
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:18,800
Come on, please.

264
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:22,161
Please?

265
00:20:22,992 --> 00:20:24,080
It was because of Tong.

266
00:20:35,238 --> 00:20:36,360
Your ex?

267
00:20:38,288 --> 00:20:39,289
Yeah.

268
00:20:40,550 --> 00:20:42,120
Tong invited me to take art lessons.

269
00:20:47,360 --> 00:20:50,502
See? This is why I didn't want to tell you.

270
00:20:52,590 --> 00:20:54,203
You once told me

271
00:20:54,579 --> 00:20:56,979
that your father had chosen a path
for each of his children.

272
00:20:58,580 --> 00:20:59,720
What did he choose for you?

273
00:21:05,720 --> 00:21:06,721
I don't know either.

274
00:21:08,070 --> 00:21:09,240
Dad's never told me.

275
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:14,500
It's different with Yi and Big.

276
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,550
Dad had Yi learn the family
business from a young age.

277
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:21,640
As for Big,

278
00:21:22,702 --> 00:21:24,462
Dad had him train to
become a police officer

279
00:21:24,800 --> 00:21:26,920
so he could handle things
whenever there was trouble.

280
00:21:30,392 --> 00:21:31,393
But as for me,

281
00:21:37,902 --> 00:21:40,400
maybe Dad doesn't think
I have any special talents.

282
00:21:42,603 --> 00:21:45,480
That's a good thing.
It means you get to choose for yourself.

283
00:21:50,358 --> 00:21:51,359
I may get to choose,

284
00:21:51,771 --> 00:21:53,920
but that doesn't mean things will work out.

285
00:22:03,550 --> 00:22:04,551
Just hypothetically...

286
00:22:05,715 --> 00:22:07,395
what if we couldn't be together in person?

287
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:11,041
What if I stayed here

288
00:22:12,224 --> 00:22:14,040
while you went to study in Bangkok?

289
00:22:15,931 --> 00:22:16,932
Do you think...

290
00:22:18,032 --> 00:22:19,400
we'd still be together?

291
00:22:20,406 --> 00:22:23,000
Even if we had to live apart

292
00:22:23,915 --> 00:22:25,920
and have a long-distance
relationship instead?

293
00:22:27,872 --> 00:22:29,360
Do we really have to break up?

294
00:22:30,120 --> 00:22:31,640
I don't want to do long-distance.

295
00:22:40,032 --> 00:22:41,592
But I was only speaking hypothetically.

296
00:22:41,979 --> 00:22:44,161
No matter what, I'm going with you.

297
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:46,700
I'll just close my eyes and pick a program.

298
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:49,240
There must be one I can
get into with my scores.

299
00:22:51,771 --> 00:22:52,772
Please don't.

300
00:22:56,206 --> 00:22:59,160
I don't want you not choosing
your dream because of me.

301
00:23:00,968 --> 00:23:02,360
If you rush into making a choice

302
00:23:03,336 --> 00:23:05,000
and regret it later,

303
00:23:05,902 --> 00:23:07,800
you might end up resenting me for it.

304
00:23:11,459 --> 00:23:13,850
I want you to choose for yourself.

305
00:23:14,366 --> 00:23:16,560
But the problem is, I don't
have any other dreams.

306
00:23:20,984 --> 00:23:22,600
You're my dream.

307
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:40,121
[Singing off-key.]

308
00:23:49,592 --> 00:23:50,940
Everyone.

309
00:23:52,323 --> 00:23:55,400
Today, a representative
from Chanthara Suksa

310
00:23:55,424 --> 00:23:57,040
will be joining our rehearsal.

311
00:23:57,280 --> 00:23:59,243
Our opening performance

312
00:23:59,291 --> 00:24:01,051
will feature both bands
performing together.

313
00:24:02,144 --> 00:24:03,590
Oh, perfect timing.

314
00:24:03,824 --> 00:24:04,825
Come on over.

315
00:24:16,232 --> 00:24:17,360
Everyone, this is Tong.

316
00:24:17,486 --> 00:24:19,360
Stand here so everyone can see you clearly.

317
00:24:19,710 --> 00:24:22,720
Tong Nattapong is
representing Chanthara Suksa.

318
00:24:22,819 --> 00:24:24,499
Why don't you all get to know one another?

319
00:24:25,072 --> 00:24:26,720
Please make him feel welcome.

320
00:24:29,603 --> 00:24:32,480
Let's work on the sets
and props outside today.

321
00:24:33,155 --> 00:24:35,100
That way, we won't
disturb the band's rehearsal.

322
00:24:43,131 --> 00:24:44,310
Oh, hi.

323
00:24:44,859 --> 00:24:46,300
- Hello.
- Tong, right?

324
00:24:46,390 --> 00:24:48,520
- Yeah.
- I'm Jai, I'm the leader of the school band.

325
00:24:48,603 --> 00:24:49,604
I'm also a lead singer.

326
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:51,312
Oh, you were great earlier.

327
00:24:51,429 --> 00:24:52,430
Tong.

328
00:24:52,600 --> 00:24:55,120
Why don't you rehearse with
the band's backup vocalists?

329
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:57,200
What do you mean, ma'am?

330
00:24:57,891 --> 00:24:59,960
Jiwara, why are you still
sitting there? Come on.

331
00:25:00,019 --> 00:25:01,020
Come rehearse.

332
00:25:03,020 --> 00:25:04,160
Here's the thing.

333
00:25:04,774 --> 00:25:07,440
The principal considers this a major event,

334
00:25:07,475 --> 00:25:09,276
and the school's reputation is at stake.

335
00:25:09,472 --> 00:25:11,752
You're not suitable to be
the lead singer for this event.

336
00:25:11,830 --> 00:25:13,920
But you can't do this, ma'am.

337
00:25:14,131 --> 00:25:15,920
I've been rehearsing
for this event all year.

338
00:25:15,932 --> 00:25:17,902
You can't just replace me
whenever you feel like it.

339
00:25:17,926 --> 00:25:19,720
You need to accept the truth, Sophawan.

340
00:25:19,846 --> 00:25:22,520
You were never suited to
be the school's lead singer.

341
00:25:22,850 --> 00:25:25,290
You should know how you got
that position in the first place.

342
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:27,840
- I'll be right back.
- Okay.

343
00:25:35,139 --> 00:25:36,140
Blue.

344
00:25:36,403 --> 00:25:37,859
Blue!

345
00:25:39,832 --> 00:25:40,992
Why the hell did you do that?

346
00:25:41,646 --> 00:25:43,680
What? Long time no see.

347
00:25:43,838 --> 00:25:45,326
Aren't you going to say hello properly?

348
00:25:45,350 --> 00:25:46,710
Are you trying to start something?

349
00:25:46,982 --> 00:25:48,640
Why did you have to follow me here?

350
00:25:49,542 --> 00:25:51,760
Well, you gave me the idea.

351
00:25:51,899 --> 00:25:53,560
I want to be a part of the
university admissions quota too.

352
00:25:54,758 --> 00:25:55,759
That's ridiculous.

353
00:25:56,643 --> 00:25:58,700
You were already a
school athlete back there.

354
00:25:59,536 --> 00:26:01,136
What quota could you possibly need here?

355
00:26:01,528 --> 00:26:02,929
Stop making excuses.

356
00:26:07,883 --> 00:26:08,884
The truth is...

357
00:26:10,086 --> 00:26:11,600
I want you to give me another chance.

358
00:26:13,414 --> 00:26:15,240
You said you didn't like
long-distance relationships, remember?

359
00:26:15,260 --> 00:26:16,720
Now I've moved closer to you.

360
00:26:17,790 --> 00:26:19,270
Can we start seeing each other again?

361
00:26:20,142 --> 00:26:22,542
Breaking up because of
the distance wasn't fair to me, Blue.

362
00:26:25,326 --> 00:26:26,327
Forget it.

363
00:26:27,527 --> 00:26:28,800
That second chance you want?

364
00:26:30,264 --> 00:26:31,424
I don't have one to give you.

365
00:26:37,080 --> 00:26:38,520
Is it because you're dating someone?

366
00:26:43,275 --> 00:26:44,515
That has nothing to do with it.

367
00:26:45,792 --> 00:26:47,160
What's over

368
00:26:48,174 --> 00:26:49,200
is over.

369
00:26:52,670 --> 00:26:53,681
I'm not giving up.

370
00:26:55,214 --> 00:26:56,360
I'll show you

371
00:26:56,380 --> 00:26:57,980
that being with me is the better choice.

372
00:26:59,979 --> 00:27:01,139
Pretty confident, aren't you?

373
00:27:17,347 --> 00:27:18,840
That was Tong, wasn't it?

374
00:27:21,032 --> 00:27:22,033
Yeah.

375
00:27:23,344 --> 00:27:24,680
But I didn't invite him here.

376
00:27:26,128 --> 00:27:27,200
He came on his own.

377
00:27:30,875 --> 00:27:31,876
I didn't say you did.

378
00:27:33,147 --> 00:27:35,614
But once this event is over,
you won't be seeing him again, right?

379
00:27:35,638 --> 00:27:36,639
Right?

380
00:28:28,224 --> 00:28:29,720
I'd like Police Commander Sin

381
00:28:30,326 --> 00:28:33,040
to look after and protect me and my family,

382
00:28:34,160 --> 00:28:36,680
just as you would any
other citizens in this province.

383
00:28:44,123 --> 00:28:45,124
What?

384
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:49,136
The police got a tip
about our gambling den.

385
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:51,320
Police Commander Sin said
we've been operating too openly.

386
00:28:51,344 --> 00:28:54,064
We have to shut it down for now.
The police are raiding it tomorrow.

387
00:28:57,408 --> 00:28:58,960
If you're this useless,

388
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:03,913
why the hell did I pay all those bribes
to get you into the police force?

389
00:29:07,336 --> 00:29:08,976
They're coming down hard on us this time.

390
00:29:10,264 --> 00:29:12,344
They made a deal directly
with Police Commander Sin.

391
00:29:15,757 --> 00:29:18,176
The influential officials who took side with
the family that won the port concession,

392
00:29:18,200 --> 00:29:19,201
you should...

393
00:29:27,979 --> 00:29:31,120
What the fuck is Commander
Sin playing at? That bastard!

394
00:29:33,560 --> 00:29:36,760
He told us to lay low with the gambling den
and the underground lottery for now.

395
00:29:39,382 --> 00:29:40,383
More importantly,

396
00:29:43,190 --> 00:29:44,960
he ordered us to stay
away from that family.

397
00:29:45,369 --> 00:29:47,960
That fucking Commander Sin
talked to us like we were dirt.

398
00:29:48,680 --> 00:29:51,040
Does he plan on returning
any of the money we paid him?

399
00:29:51,235 --> 00:29:53,275
We should be grateful he
isn't demanding even more.

400
00:29:53,448 --> 00:29:56,149
This is because you went
after Wiboon's daughter.

401
00:29:57,280 --> 00:29:58,881
You handed them an opening to attack us.

402
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:01,837
Don't you understand that
we can't shut down the gambling den

403
00:30:01,861 --> 00:30:03,280
and the underground lottery?

404
00:30:03,430 --> 00:30:05,431
I need that cash to keep
our men on our side.

405
00:30:05,700 --> 00:30:07,656
What are you gonna do if all our men
switch sides and join the Monchaitrakuls?

406
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:09,616
I've told you not to buy
your men's loyalty with money.

407
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:10,641
Do you ever listen to me?

408
00:30:10,790 --> 00:30:12,960
- Use your brain for once...
- Shhh.

409
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:14,241
Enough.

410
00:30:20,040 --> 00:30:21,041
Hey,

411
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:33,600
I'm gonna take this one.

412
00:30:43,835 --> 00:30:45,240
Come on.

413
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:47,280
It's okay.

414
00:30:48,011 --> 00:30:49,971
It's okay if you're not
the school's lead singer.

415
00:30:50,680 --> 00:30:53,940
Honestly, it's not that surprising.

416
00:30:54,360 --> 00:30:56,440
Anyone who's heard you
sing could've seen it coming.

417
00:30:56,971 --> 00:30:58,720
I think the only reason
they gave you the position

418
00:30:58,740 --> 00:31:01,080
was because the teachers
didn't want to upset Tokyo.

419
00:31:01,960 --> 00:31:03,840
Why do you have to rub it in?

420
00:31:04,246 --> 00:31:07,360
Yeah, I know I sing off-key.

421
00:31:07,664 --> 00:31:09,840
And it was shitty of me to use Tokyo's name

422
00:31:09,865 --> 00:31:11,512
to get myself made
the school's lead singer.

423
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:14,000
But so what? I still worked hard, didn't I?

424
00:31:15,195 --> 00:31:18,360
You know I practiced every single day.

425
00:31:20,904 --> 00:31:23,280
Hey, it's okay, Jai.

426
00:31:25,038 --> 00:31:26,720
You could always sing on TikTok.

427
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:28,520
That won't work.

428
00:31:30,408 --> 00:31:32,368
I need the school singer
position on my portfolio

429
00:31:32,409 --> 00:31:34,129
to apply for the university admissions quota.

430
00:31:34,632 --> 00:31:36,592
If they take the position
away from me like this,

431
00:31:37,096 --> 00:31:39,280
my chances are practically zero.

432
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:43,200
Who's going to take responsibility
for all the work I've put in?

433
00:31:45,342 --> 00:31:46,800
I'm sure it'll be okay.

434
00:31:46,870 --> 00:31:49,170
We'll find another way.

435
00:31:49,530 --> 00:31:52,690
And if you're truly determined, you
can still get in through the entrance exam.

436
00:31:54,080 --> 00:31:56,920
Hey. It'll be okay.

437
00:32:07,696 --> 00:32:09,400
When my braid is on the left,

438
00:32:10,360 --> 00:32:12,080
that's your cue to meet me in the bathroom.

439
00:32:16,774 --> 00:32:17,856
And…

440
00:32:19,096 --> 00:32:20,440
What about the right side?

441
00:32:35,100 --> 00:32:36,101
You need to meet me here.

442
00:32:43,766 --> 00:32:44,891
And…

443
00:32:45,904 --> 00:32:47,005
What if...

444
00:32:50,547 --> 00:32:51,800
I want to kiss you like this?

445
00:32:53,600 --> 00:32:55,360
There's no secret code for that.

446
00:32:57,539 --> 00:32:59,640
If you can't figure it out,

447
00:33:03,701 --> 00:33:04,702
then it's your loss.

448
00:33:12,328 --> 00:33:13,329
Your loss.

449
00:33:32,782 --> 00:33:34,480
Blue.

450
00:33:39,763 --> 00:33:41,443
I know you don't want to talk to me, Blue.

451
00:33:42,110 --> 00:33:44,000
But I know the reason
you won't take me back.

452
00:33:47,411 --> 00:33:49,051
It's because you are dating someone, right?

453
00:33:52,390 --> 00:33:53,391
It's Tokyo, isn't it?

454
00:34:07,816 --> 00:34:10,278
Whether it's true or not,
it's none of your business.

455
00:34:12,627 --> 00:34:13,628
No, it isn't.

456
00:34:14,195 --> 00:34:15,840
But aren't your families enemies?

457
00:34:17,680 --> 00:34:19,880
I know you probably don't
care what your father thinks,

458
00:34:20,579 --> 00:34:22,930
but I've heard Tokyo's
family can be pretty ruthless.

459
00:34:25,160 --> 00:34:26,161
Are you threatening me?

460
00:34:28,290 --> 00:34:29,291
No.

461
00:34:29,573 --> 00:34:30,574
But...

462
00:34:30,580 --> 00:34:32,900
if you don't want me
telling your family or Tokyo's,

463
00:34:34,040 --> 00:34:35,441
then give me another chance.

464
00:35:10,995 --> 00:35:12,640
♪ Because I've never ♪

465
00:35:12,851 --> 00:35:16,120
♪ Been good with words ♪

466
00:35:16,659 --> 00:35:21,660
♪ You know that better than anyone ♪

467
00:35:22,219 --> 00:35:27,200
♪ And the reason I never say ♪

468
00:35:27,350 --> 00:35:31,850
♪ The sweet, heartfelt things others do ♪

469
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:35,080
♪ Is because I believe a love song ♪

470
00:35:35,181 --> 00:35:37,600
♪ Dedicated to you ♪

471
00:35:37,755 --> 00:35:42,840
♪ Should be one song, and one song alone ♪

472
00:35:43,787 --> 00:35:46,840
♪ If there were too many ♪

473
00:35:47,107 --> 00:35:49,560
♪ All those tender words ♪

474
00:35:49,608 --> 00:35:54,909
♪ Might begin to lose their meaning ♪

475
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:57,740
♪ I want you to know ♪

476
00:36:00,558 --> 00:36:02,440
Blue, is Tong hitting on you?

477
00:36:03,006 --> 00:36:05,200
A new couple in the making. Here we go.

478
00:36:13,272 --> 00:36:15,040
Actually, I'm not here to hit on Blue.

479
00:36:16,913 --> 00:36:18,220
I'm Blue's ex.

480
00:36:19,176 --> 00:36:20,840
I came here to ask her to take me back.

481
00:36:22,413 --> 00:36:25,160
Shit. Is he your favorite ex or something?

482
00:36:25,288 --> 00:36:27,120
Well, Blue? What are
you gonna do? Tell him.

483
00:36:29,000 --> 00:36:30,001
For sure.

484
00:36:45,035 --> 00:36:46,200
Let's rehearse again.

485
00:36:55,904 --> 00:36:56,905
Here.

486
00:36:57,560 --> 00:36:58,800
It's the cheesecake you like.

487
00:37:00,600 --> 00:37:01,601
Thanks.

488
00:37:04,470 --> 00:37:05,720
But I don't like it anymore.

489
00:37:08,576 --> 00:37:10,300
Are you still mad at me?

490
00:37:11,152 --> 00:37:12,160
I'm sorry.

491
00:37:12,899 --> 00:37:15,200
Can we start over?

492
00:37:16,552 --> 00:37:18,840
It has nothing to do
with you threatening me.

493
00:37:20,360 --> 00:37:21,640
But you know that doing all this

494
00:37:22,032 --> 00:37:24,320
still won't make me take you back, right?

495
00:37:26,976 --> 00:37:30,080
And I'm not angry that
you followed me here.

496
00:37:32,587 --> 00:37:34,336
Because I know the
school you transferred to

497
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:36,360
really is known for its
athletic admissions quota.

498
00:37:40,288 --> 00:37:41,289
What I am angry about

499
00:37:42,830 --> 00:37:44,300
is that you tried to blackmail me.

500
00:37:45,360 --> 00:37:46,700
- Please, Blue...
- Tong.

501
00:37:47,650 --> 00:37:50,440
Believe it or not, before all this,

502
00:37:50,830 --> 00:37:52,600
I thought that once I went back home,

503
00:37:52,936 --> 00:37:55,640
I could still text you and
talk to you like before.

504
00:37:55,694 --> 00:37:56,894
I thought we could be friends.

505
00:37:58,220 --> 00:37:59,221
But now,

506
00:38:00,094 --> 00:38:01,894
I don't want anything
to do with you anymore.

507
00:38:02,298 --> 00:38:05,280
But I only did it because I
wanted to keep you safe.

508
00:38:06,611 --> 00:38:08,147
Your mom told me everything

509
00:38:08,184 --> 00:38:09,760
about how dangerous that family is.

510
00:38:11,240 --> 00:38:13,840
What you and Tokyo
are doing really isn't safe.

511
00:38:14,877 --> 00:38:17,720
Tokyo could end up in danger too.

512
00:38:18,878 --> 00:38:19,880
Please believe me.

513
00:38:21,693 --> 00:38:23,100
Don't put yourself at risk.

514
00:38:25,160 --> 00:38:26,440
I'll protect you.

515
00:38:37,723 --> 00:38:38,724
Sorry.

516
00:38:39,931 --> 00:38:41,640
We're better off staying exes.

517
00:39:29,080 --> 00:39:32,360
♪ On a night with no stars in the sky ♪

518
00:39:32,560 --> 00:39:34,960
♪ Just another ordinary night ♪

519
00:39:35,061 --> 00:39:40,560
♪ Nothing around us is setting the mood ♪

520
00:39:40,960 --> 00:39:43,520
♪ I want to reach out and hold your hand ♪

521
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:45,001
What is it?

522
00:39:47,995 --> 00:39:49,360
What is going on?

523
00:39:49,376 --> 00:39:52,280
Come on, don't be shy. Just look at him.

524
00:39:52,523 --> 00:39:54,000
♪ Because I've never ♪

525
00:39:54,124 --> 00:39:57,400
♪ Been good with words ♪

526
00:39:57,890 --> 00:40:01,920
♪ You know that better than anyone ♪

527
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:04,640
Hey, it's okay.

528
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:06,560
We can always start our own band later.

529
00:40:07,189 --> 00:40:08,190
Right?

530
00:40:09,232 --> 00:40:10,520
We should be worried about Tokyo instead.

531
00:40:10,533 --> 00:40:11,893
Who knows where the hell she went?

532
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:15,080
She was so shocked
that she just disappeared.

533
00:40:19,198 --> 00:40:24,100
♪ Should be one song, and one song alone ♪

534
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:27,840
♪ If there were too many ♪

535
00:40:28,320 --> 00:40:30,640
♪ All those tender words ♪

536
00:40:31,142 --> 00:40:35,360
♪ Might begin to lose their meaning ♪

537
00:40:36,480 --> 00:40:38,481
♪ I want you to know ♪

538
00:40:39,160 --> 00:40:42,520
♪ Let our eyes do the talking ♪

539
00:40:43,360 --> 00:40:45,560
♪ Every time our gazes meet ♪

540
00:40:46,165 --> 00:40:47,166
Ouch!

541
00:40:48,878 --> 00:40:49,879
Ow!

542
00:40:50,720 --> 00:40:51,721
Let me go!

543
00:40:52,920 --> 00:40:53,921
Who are you?

544
00:41:00,360 --> 00:41:01,361
Tokyo?

545
00:41:09,203 --> 00:41:10,920
You didn't show up that day

546
00:41:11,768 --> 00:41:14,208
because you were afraid someone
would see us together, right?

547
00:41:15,059 --> 00:41:16,979
If it was because Tong
threatened you like that,

548
00:41:17,341 --> 00:41:19,181
I've already talked to
Tong and sorted it out.

549
00:41:26,614 --> 00:41:27,615
Can I give you a hand?

550
00:41:31,120 --> 00:41:32,840
It's okay. I can do this.

551
00:41:34,011 --> 00:41:35,611
I've already asked Blue to take me back.

552
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:39,640
The reason I moved here

553
00:41:39,680 --> 00:41:41,181
is because Blue's mother asked me to.

554
00:41:43,700 --> 00:41:45,920
She wants Blue and me to get back together.

555
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:48,760
Let me ask you something.

556
00:41:49,715 --> 00:41:52,250
What exactly are you to Blue?

557
00:41:53,603 --> 00:41:54,680
Whatever I am,

558
00:41:55,502 --> 00:41:57,003
I'm more than an ex like you.

559
00:41:59,174 --> 00:42:00,640
You do realize that you're just

560
00:42:00,837 --> 00:42:02,040
dragging Blue into

561
00:42:02,138 --> 00:42:03,778
the feud between our families, don't you?

562
00:42:04,523 --> 00:42:06,083
You're making things difficult for her.

563
00:42:06,966 --> 00:42:08,360
If you truly care about Blue,

564
00:42:09,167 --> 00:42:10,280
then let her go.

565
00:42:26,145 --> 00:42:28,093
If that's your idea of threatening me,

566
00:42:28,776 --> 00:42:29,920
you need to try harder.

567
00:42:30,875 --> 00:42:31,920
You know.

568
00:42:32,704 --> 00:42:34,480
I was raised in a mafia family.

569
00:42:35,584 --> 00:42:37,000
Something like this won't scare me.

570
00:42:38,120 --> 00:42:40,880
And stop using the
adults' feud as an excuse.

571
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:43,800
We can handle

572
00:42:44,280 --> 00:42:45,520
our own relationships.

573
00:42:46,899 --> 00:42:48,099
We don't need you interfering.

574
00:43:12,254 --> 00:43:13,840
But none of that matters now.

575
00:43:16,411 --> 00:43:17,412
I...

576
00:43:17,840 --> 00:43:20,120
I really don't need you
to do anything for me.

577
00:43:23,547 --> 00:43:27,080
And I don't want the adults
involved in anything between us,

578
00:43:28,640 --> 00:43:29,641
whether it's school

579
00:43:30,600 --> 00:43:31,760
or our relationship.

580
00:43:37,500 --> 00:43:38,501
I...

581
00:43:39,275 --> 00:43:41,560
I don't have any grand dreams like you,

582
00:43:43,320 --> 00:43:44,321
like Jai,

583
00:43:45,438 --> 00:43:47,040
or like our other friends.

584
00:43:50,864 --> 00:43:52,300
I just know

585
00:43:54,160 --> 00:43:55,440
that I want to be with you.

586
00:43:56,761 --> 00:43:58,200
And I want the freedom

587
00:43:59,077 --> 00:44:00,360
to make my own choices.

588
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:03,001
That's all.

589
00:44:08,059 --> 00:44:10,640
We're not going to break up

590
00:44:13,013 --> 00:44:14,014
because of anyone else.

591
00:44:16,022 --> 00:44:17,280
If we ever do break up,

592
00:44:19,979 --> 00:44:22,139
it should be because we
don't love each other anymore.

593
00:44:23,736 --> 00:44:24,737
Okay?

594
00:44:46,352 --> 00:44:47,840
♪ To you ♪

595
00:44:50,080 --> 00:44:52,120
♪ The one who means everything to me ♪

596
00:44:54,384 --> 00:44:58,320
♪ I'll be waiting to walk beside you ♪

597
00:45:00,144 --> 00:45:02,760
♪ Our dreams won't be far away ♪

598
00:45:03,926 --> 00:45:05,080
♪ But you ♪

599
00:45:07,531 --> 00:45:11,400
♪ slowly faded away and changed ♪

600
00:45:11,960 --> 00:45:15,560
♪ My journey toward my
dreams came to an end ♪

601
00:45:17,609 --> 00:45:20,320
♪ No matter how long it takes ♪

602
00:45:21,357 --> 00:45:24,720
♪ I keep waiting ♪

603
00:45:26,123 --> 00:45:27,800
♪ I'll be waiting ♪

604
00:45:28,459 --> 00:45:31,080
♪ Though it may be only a dream ♪

605
00:45:31,798 --> 00:45:35,799
♪ Of a better day ♪

606
00:45:37,080 --> 00:45:39,640
♪ When you return to me ♪

607
00:45:40,081 --> 00:45:44,240
♪ There'll be love and everything we need ♪

608
00:45:44,539 --> 00:45:48,400
♪ There'll be dreams
at the end of the road ♪

609
00:45:48,540 --> 00:45:52,920
♪ There'll be the two of
us, walking side by side ♪

610
00:45:56,355 --> 00:45:57,440
♪ To you ♪

611
00:45:57,752 --> 00:46:01,440
♪ Who give love depth ♪

612
00:46:02,040 --> 00:46:06,160
♪ Who'll lead me to where I belong ♪

613
00:46:06,550 --> 00:46:10,480
♪ There'll be love and everything we need ♪

614
00:46:13,744 --> 00:46:15,200
♪ To you ♪

615
00:46:15,248 --> 00:46:19,280
♪ There'll be love and everything we need ♪

616
00:46:19,552 --> 00:46:23,360
♪ There'll be dreams
at the end of the road ♪

617
00:46:23,664 --> 00:46:28,000
♪ There'll be the two of
us, walking side by side ♪

618
00:46:31,206 --> 00:46:32,360
♪ To you ♪

619
00:46:32,645 --> 00:46:36,560
♪ Who give love depth ♪

620
00:46:37,029 --> 00:46:40,960
♪ Who'll lead me to where I belong ♪

621
00:46:41,408 --> 00:46:44,000
♪ You're the one who made my love... ♪

622
00:46:46,792 --> 00:46:48,500
♪ become real ♪

623
00:47:24,659 --> 00:47:25,660
[Next Episode]
Tokyo.

624
00:47:27,304 --> 00:47:28,320
We need to talk.

625
00:47:28,734 --> 00:47:30,480
How dare you do this to us?

626
00:47:30,973 --> 00:47:32,520
You're betraying our family.

627
00:47:35,680 --> 00:47:37,280
If we don't do something now,

628
00:47:37,752 --> 00:47:39,680
we'll be stuck here
for the rest of our lives.

629
00:47:48,976 --> 00:47:50,120
If you don't stop,

630
00:47:50,336 --> 00:47:51,600
I'll show you

631
00:47:51,920 --> 00:47:54,000
exactly what the eldest
son of the Kongpurim family

632
00:47:54,118 --> 00:47:55,238
is capable of shutting down.
